                                   \n                                        \n${e}^{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$\\int h(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139533791 true] [17592186251483 1113 #uuid "e934691b-0128-5cb9-9f67-814123c43489" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251483 1145 "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int h(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139533791 true] [17592186251484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251485 13194139533791 true] [17592186251484 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533791 true] [17592186251484 1041 "field-1" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251484 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251485 13194139533791 true] [17592186251484 1110 #uuid "68116713-acce-576f-ac38-3804758b2e18" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251485 1034 "4\\cos(x)" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533791 true] [17592186251485 1111 #uuid "f8edfd58-bdbc-5fbb-abb9-7adf13d93e37" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251486 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251487 13194139533791 true] [17592186251486 1089 "q-167332" 13194139533791 true] [17592186251486 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533791 true] [17592186251486 1100 "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4\\cos(x)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\n${g}^{″}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4x$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nIf a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Slope $\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2e^{\\pi}$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nThe equation of the normal to the curve $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x)$ at the point where $x=\\pi $ is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,y=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{\\pi-x}{2e^{\\pi}}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\